title: Faction Caucus
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: caucus_timer <= 0
on-arrival: caucus_timer = 4; month_actions += 1

= Faction Caucus

The Federation only holds together if each of its wings feels heard. Whose concerns should get the floor at this month's caucus?

- @caucus_socialists: The Socialists.
- @caucus_populists: The Populists.
- @caucus_unionists: The Industrial Unionists.
- @caucus_progressives: The Progressives.

@caucus_socialists
on-arrival: {!
Q.socialists_strength += 3;
Q.socialists_dissent = Math.max(0, Q.socialists_dissent - 6);
Q.populists_strength -= 1; Q.unionists_strength -= 1; Q.progressives_strength -= 1;
Q.urban_ethnic_fl += 1;
Q.small_town_fl -= 1;
!}

Norman Thomas holds forth for two hours on the co-operative commonwealth. The organizers leave the room energized. The moderates leave it checking their watches.

@caucus_populists
on-arrival: {!
Q.populists_strength += 3;
Q.populists_dissent = Math.max(0, Q.populists_dissent - 6);
Q.socialists_strength -= 1; Q.unionists_strength -= 1; Q.progressives_strength -= 1;
Q.farmers_fl += 1;
!}

Robert La Follette Jr. and Governor Olson lay out a programme of grain elevators, public banks and freight rates. It is the most practical hour of the year, and the farm delegations go home satisfied.

@caucus_unionists
on-arrival: {!
Q.unionists_strength += 3;
Q.unionists_dissent = Math.max(0, Q.unionists_dissent - 6);
Q.socialists_strength -= 1; Q.populists_strength -= 1; Q.progressives_strength -= 1;
Q.tradesmen_fl += 1;
!}

John L. Lewis, Sidney Hillman and Philip Murray come with a list of bargaining demands and a clear message about who pays for the party's campaigns. Nobody argues.

@caucus_progressives
on-arrival: {!
Q.progressives_strength += 3;
Q.progressives_dissent = Math.max(0, Q.progressives_dissent - 6);
Q.socialists_strength -= 1; Q.populists_strength -= 1; Q.unionists_strength -= 1;
Q.small_town_fl += 1;
!}

La Guardia and Ickes come armed with ledgers documenting municipal graft and a proposal for direct democracy. The middle-class reformers are delighted, and the socialists mutter about half-measures.
